Aim

To create Docker images using Dockerfile and run applications inside containers.

Theory (Short)

A Dockerfile is a text file that contains instructions to build a Docker image.
It defines base image, application files, and execution commands.
Docker builds an image from Dockerfile and runs it as a container.

Steps
Step 1: Create Project Folder
mkdir docker-app
cd docker-app
Step 2: Create Java File

Hello.java

public class Hello {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello Docker");
    }
}
Step 3: Create Dockerfile
FROM openjdk:17
COPY . /app
WORKDIR /app
RUN javac Hello.java
CMD ["java", "Hello"]
Step 4: Build Docker Image
docker build -t hello-docker .
Step 5: Run Docker Container
docker run hello-docker

Output:

Hello Docker
Step 6: Check Images
docker images
Result

Docker image was successfully created and executed using Dockerfile.
